The Dark Energy Spectroscopic Instrument (DESI) and the Simons Observatory (SO) are well-positioned for cross-correlation analyses. Previous DESI+CMB analyses have focused on baryon acoustic oscillation (BAO) measurements or the growth rate of structure. Analyses using cosmological lensing ratios -- geometric quantities containing only information about the universe's expansion history -- have not yet been performed. We forecast constraints on cosmology from DESI$\times$SO analyses focused on these ratios, and find them to be competitive with constraints from pre-existing DESI BAO+CMB analyses. 

The main forecasting results are in SOxDESI_forecasting.ipynb, with functions and classes taken from functions_and_classes. Fisher and covariance matrices are in the Fisher Forecasts folder, plots in the plots folder, and MCMC chains in the chains folder. 